// The settings tab: nine unrelated jobs, nine components, one page.
//
// They share a tab because an operator thinks of them as "the shop's own controls", not
// because they share any state - each loads and saves independently, so one failing to load
// does not blank the others, and each form sends ONLY its own fields. The server treats an
// absent field as unchanged, which is what makes that safe: saving SMS settings cannot
// touch the merchant id, and neither can touch the tether rate.
//
// THE GATEWAY AND THE SMS PANEL ARE APART because they fail apart - a broken SMS key stops
// delivery, a wrong merchant id sends the takings to
// a stranger - and an operator fixing one should never be editing a form that can save the
// other. The shop NAME sits in its own card above both for the same reason: it is the tab
// title, the SMS text AND the transaction description, so it belongs to neither.
//
// Every one of these changes something that costs money, access, or secrecy, and each guards
// itself: the merchant id asks for confirmation, the rate and the margin ask too (they
// multiply every card at once), a tier removal says which of the two things it did, sending
// the database to Telegram asks before it does it, and rotating the key demands the current
// one even though a session is already open.
//
// THE ENGLISH SHOP'S TWO CARDS - NOWPayments and Resend - sit after the Persian shop's gateway and
// SMS panel, in the same order: how a buyer pays, then how their code reaches them.
//
// PRICING SITS SECOND, right under the catalogue. The cards above it no longer carry prices -
// they carry denominations - so the panel that explains what those cost belongs next to them
// rather than below the gateway credentials.
import AdminShell from '../shell.azeroth';
import TierSettings from './tiers.azeroth';
import PricingSettings from './pricing.azeroth';
import ShopSettings from './shop.azeroth';
import GatewaySettings from './gateway.azeroth';
import SmsSettings from './sms.azeroth';
import NowPaymentsSettings from './nowpayments.azeroth';
import EmailSettings from './email.azeroth';
import TelegramSettings from './telegram.azeroth';
import AdminKeySettings from './admin-key.azeroth';

export default component AdminSettings()
{
    <AdminShell>
        <TierSettings />
        <PricingSettings />
        <ShopSettings />
        <GatewaySettings />
        <SmsSettings />
        <NowPaymentsSettings />
        <EmailSettings />
        <TelegramSettings />
        <AdminKeySettings />
    </AdminShell>
}
